drm/omap: send only the damage to a manually updated display

Every update of the N8x0's RFBI display sent the whole frame, 42 ms at
800x480 over the bus to the S1D13745, which keeps its own copy of the
frame. Send only what changed, as Nokia's omapfb did (blizzard.c,
do_partial_update()):

- the primary plane takes FB_DAMAGE_CLIPS; alone on a manually updated
  CRTC, covering it unscaled and unrotated, it fetches just the merged
  damage (whole 8-pixel columns) and the CRTC's output size follows it;
- a DSI op, update_rect(), sends a rectangle; RFBI implements it, and
  its client (the S1D1374x) sets its input window to the rectangle and
  the output window to it, scaled in the half-size mode;
- DIRTYFB goes through drm_atomic_helper_dirtyfb(), so its clips (and
  fbdev's damage) become damage too; it used to send whole frames.

